tion/answer-fields ["q-49674/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49674"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-349297/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "fa6ddf20-2c4e-5339-9f97-9782ac10c944" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-349297/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6660f982-ce9e-5cdb-bd76-ec38a76c647d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-349297/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-349297/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-349297" :question/id #uuid "104a55a5-693b-5c53-8ef0-cafe5e29693f" :question/math-academy-id "q-349297" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}9x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=9x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=9 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & ⇒ & v=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 9x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =9x\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\int \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\cdot 9\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}9x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3}-3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =3(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\cdot 0-0\\cdot 0)+(-1-1) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-349297/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-349297"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49660/selection/146cabb1e263080a1e44d68392e0feef4ec0cd9580855b924fffd3772b057cbd" :answer/id #uuid "6ec45187-f1eb-5762-bc52-0346ef62c508" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2-{e}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49660/selection/9ca3fff028d1d6ce270e6ee452d64a1003a4bb96ed712d608753a9391e148eb4" :answer/id #uuid "e9c8873c-e846-535c-974e-1e7cb0f4edec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-3{e}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49660/selection/301bedc4cb42c0433b80e059562b9af7c6f2793fe0bc12128137f85bcd0f677a" :answer/id #uuid "79884932-1291-545f-9074-499a42fc8d05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+{e}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49660/selection/dbbb98b1a0d3894cc5be8aa494b846c4880f9bca12ba750494eded5e7b0ad73b" :answer/id #uuid "e70e8dbd-5827-511d-a205-b64b96acb6b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1+{e}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49660/selection/0f75fc4fb2c9da235fdad92564cae4d5adfe303b5e94a835680de48601c7afb1" :answer/id #uuid "47159201-f331-5c83-8ddc-383828eab39e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1-{e}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49660/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "194e6f4a-2d92-5da0-9dac-d53c5bf8c3a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49660/selection/0f75fc4fb2c9da235fdad92564cae4d5adfe303b5e94a835680de48601c7afb1" :answer-field/choices ["q-49660/selection/146cabb1e263080a1e44d68392e0feef4ec0cd9580855b924fffd3772b057cbd" "q-49660/selection/9ca3fff028d1d6ce270e6ee452d64a1003a4bb96ed712d608753a9391e148eb4" "q-49660/selection/301bedc4cb42c0433b80e059562b9af7c6f2793fe0bc12128137f85bcd0f677a" "q-49660/selection/dbbb98b1a0d3894cc5be8aa494b846c4880f9bca12ba750494eded5e7b0ad73b" "q-49660/selection/0f75fc4fb2c9da235fdad92564cae4d5adfe303b5e94a835680de48601c7afb1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49660" :question/id #uuid "f7920756-127c-56a7-b85e-2c3d28bb75c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-49660" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-2}^{0}x{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & ⇒ & {u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-x} & ⇒ & v=-{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot (-{e}^{-x})-\\int (-{e}^{-x})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}x{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-x{e}^{-x}{|}_{-2}^{0}+{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x{e}^{-x}{|}_{-2}^{0}-{e}^{-x}{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =[-0{e}^{-0}-2{e}^{2}]-[{e}^{0}-{e}^{2}] \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2}-1+{e}^{2} \\\\  & =-1-{e}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49660/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49660"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49669/selection/6aa0658ec3b64327f8a2d599faa4f715c940036c4e92b012fbfb8370208f2e7d" :answer/id #uuid "66ed67ab-3b6d-5376-99af-1521eea874b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49669/selection/9c6bfb4db8d042ca3b93589c844ac1c789909e0099f428d8083546a00b4d8cf7" :answer/id #uuid "d7f549d5-ec1b-5f55-8351-0b279065d82f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49669/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "2c615c85-2408-520b-93c5-a68a79e4cd64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49669/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "281be117-ac80-5d7e-84e8-b14e444e95fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49669/selection/9700accffa78065d8053126335d2ac4e2336d0d88c76df9e6a237030f752585a" :answer/id #uuid "f480ed02-4683-599b-9ea8-e0ed4fd0efd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49669/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dce6354e-cb58-579c-8cec-f01d83452d90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49669/selection/9c6bfb4db8d042ca3b93589c844ac1c789909e0099f428d8083546a00b4d8cf7" :answer-field/choices ["q-49669/selection/6aa0658ec3b64327f8a2d599faa4f715c940036c4e92b012fbfb8370208f2e7d" "q-49669/selection/9c6bfb4db8d042ca3b93589c844ac1c789909e0099f428d8083546a00b4d8cf7" "q-49669/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-49669/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-49669/selection/9700accffa78065d8053126335d2ac4e2336d0d88c76df9e6a237030f752585a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49669" :question/id #uuid "30d59cec-59a4-58ed-913f-20fcfb228f0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-49669" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into  the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2x\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-\\int (-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={-\\frac{2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}|}_{0}^{\\pi /6}+\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={-\\frac{2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}|}_{0}^{\\pi /6}+{\\frac{2}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}[\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})-0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & +\\frac{2}{9}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}[0-0]+\\frac{2}{9}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49669/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3aaba0a-3b86-58c3-bbc8-22ced09bc8a8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49669"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-491"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv' \\, \\textrm{d}x= uv - \\int vu' \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle  \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle  \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{7x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}-\\int \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}\\int {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}(\\frac{{e}^{7x}}{7})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{49}{e}^{7x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-492"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int x \\cos{2x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x= uv- \\int vu'\\,\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int x \\cos{2x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6209"] :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{\\pi/5} x\\sin(5x) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x) & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-x\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)-\\int (-\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x))\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{1}{5}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /5}+{\\frac{1}{5}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)}{5})|}_{0}^{\\pi /5} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)]+[\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\frac{1}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)] \\\\  & =[-\\frac{\\pi }{25}\\cdot (-1)+0]+[0-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
